ainage and minimally invasive surgical debridement or endoscopic necrosectomy superior to open necrosectomy. ERCP + Sphincterotomy may be needed.", "runs": [{"text": "If stable, defer drainage to >4 weeks. If symptomatic or unstable, percutaneous drainage and minimally invasive surgical debridement or endoscopic necrosectomy superior to open necrosectomy. ERCP + Sphincterotomy may be needed."}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1488"}}, {"id": "body-09600", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Chronic Pancreatitis", "runs": [{"text": "Chronic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Pancreatitis"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1531"}}, {"id": "body-09601", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Chronic pancreatitis is long-term (chronic) inflammation of the pancreas that leads to permanent loss of function and morphology of the gland.", "runs": [{"text": "Chronic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pancreatitis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "long-term"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(chronic)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inflammation"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pancreas"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "leads"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "permanent"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "loss"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "function"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and morphology of the gland."}]}, {"id": "body-09603", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-09604", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Chronic upper abdominal pain associated with nausea, vomiting and loss of appetite.", "runs": [{"text": "Chronic"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "upper"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abdominal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text"